<title>USA: Allegheny County, Pa., seen facing $34 mln deficit.</title>
<headline>Allegheny County, Pa., seen facing $34 mln deficit.</headline>
<dateline>PITTSBURGH 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Allegheny County, Pa., could be facing a $34 million budget deficit, according to county commissioner Bob Cramner.</p>
<p>Cramner said he wants to get contract talks with the county unions settled soon, because of the union's large impact on the final budget figures.</p>
<p>Talks are said to be progressing slowly, however.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
